#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD1376 expect=violation domain=DM
#note "Pins review finding SD1376-1: the FDA sheet excludes ACTARMCD='NOTTRT' from the subjects that need RFENDTC, but the authored Check only excludes SCRNFAIL/NOTASSGN, so a NOTTRT subject with an empty RFENDTC fires. That is the SDTMIG reading (RFENDTC is required for all randomised subjects) and the complement of FDA-SD1375 — but it is an undocumented deviation from the sheet text."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-2
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 nameOnly=RFENDTC nameOnly=ACTARMCD
dataset DM label="Demographics"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col RFENDTC  type=Char label="Subject Reference End Date/Time"
col ACTARMCD type=Char label="Actual Arm Code"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | DM | 01-701-1015 |  | NOTTRT
